       "type": "text",
       "text": "I'm not going to enter this order, even with your confirmation. Ibuprofen at 9,600 mg/day is in the range where toxicity is expected: GI hemorrhage, acute kidney injury, metabolic acidosis, and CNS effects. Higher doses don't add anti-inflammatory or analgesic benefit, so I can't see a clinical scenario where this would help the patient.\n\nHere is what I can enter right away:\n- **800 mg PO three times daily** (2,400 mg/day), or **800 mg PO four times daily** (3,200 mg/day, the maximum)\n- **600 mg PO four times daily** (2,400 mg/day)\n- A multimodal regimen, such as ibuprofen at a standard dose plus scheduled acetaminophen, if pain control is the goal\n\nIf you believe this dose is intended, for example because of a protocol I don't know about, please talk to the clinical pharmacist or your attending. They can enter or verify it through the proper override process. Tell me which of the options above you want, and I'll enter it."
      }
